Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a role in a modern warehouse where every day brings new challenges? Then we have an exciting opportunity for you!

For an international logistics client in Tholen, we are looking for a Reach Truck Driver who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment, takes responsibility, and ensures that goods are stored and moved efficiently.

You will work in a dynamic environment where teamwork, safety, and quality are key. Together with your colleagues, you will help ensure that products are processed efficiently and delivered to customers around the world on time.

You are someone who enjoys working in a hands-on environment and thrives in a fast-moving warehouse setting. In addition:

✔ You have experience as a Reach Truck Driver or Logistics Employee;

✔ You have a valid reach truck certificate or are willing to obtain one;

✔ You work accurately and safely;

✔ You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.

As a Shipboard Electrician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical systems onboard ships and maritime installations. You will work with a variety of systems, including power distribution, lighting, navigation equipment, automation systems, and communication networks.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting electrical systems onboard vessels;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Inspecting, testing, and commissioning maritime electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing maintenance and repair activities on onboard systems;
- Supporting refit, modernization, and new-build projects.

You will primarily work at shipyards, ports, and onboard vessels, with occasional travel required for project support and sea trials.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field;
- Relevant experience as an electrician, preferably within shipbuilding, maritime, or offshore environments;
- Knowledge of maritime electrical systems and regulations is an advantage;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Flexible, proactive, and solution-oriented attitude;
- Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English.

As an Industrial Service Electrician, you will perform installation, maintenance, and repair work on industrial electrical systems. You will work on projects involving machinery, control cabinets, cable systems, and power installations. Safety and quality are essential in your daily work.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing industrial cabling and electrical components;
- Maintaining and testing electrical systems;
- Analyzing and solving technical faults;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings;
- Supporting project teams during installation activities.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with industrial electrical installations;
- VCA certification is preferred;
- Knowledge of industrial safety standards is an advantage;
- Flexible and hands-on mentality;
- Good command of Dutch or English.

SamenvattingDo you see a challenge in loading, unloading and carefully checking freight? Do you want to work in a dynamic, international environment? Become a Warehouse Mail Employee at Schiphol-Rijk, full-time! Good work!Over de functieAs a Warehouse Post employee, you will play an important role in loading and unloading goods and work closely with your team in a dynamic environment. Flexibility, cooperation and customer orientation are key. What will you do?
- Mail acceptance and processing;
- Sorting mail bags and parcels;
- Performing light administrative tasks;
- ULD assembly and disassembly;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Transport on the platform

You will work in a diverse team and follow a schedule with three different shifts:
- Morning shift: 07:00 - 15:30 
- Afternoon shift: 15:00 - 23:30 
- Night shift: 23:00 - 07:00 

Over het bedrijfAt this leading company, you will have the opportunity to work in a dynamic environment where teamwork and efficiency are key. As a leading player in the logistics sector, the organization offers a challenging work environment where you can further develop your skills and play an important role in the efficient handling of shipments.
Wat wij vragen- Have logistics experience;
- Willing to follow internal courses;
- Good Command of the Dutch or/and English language;
- Ready to work physically;
- You can obtain a Certificate of No Objection (VGB) ( which we will apply for) meaning you should have at least 8 years of registration within the EU.

These points are very important to start working as a Warehouse Post Employee at Schiphol-Rijk. We are also curious about who you are. Curious about your talents, background and ideas. Surprise us.
Wat wij bieden- € 16.70  € 16,99 gross salary per hour, depending on relevant work experience (including 2,5% year-end bonus) 
- Supplements for evening, night weekend shifts and public holidays, ranging from 125% to 140%
- Holiday allowances of 200%
- Weekly payments with 8.33% vac

Wat je gaat doen As a production worker, you help finish metal products with a strong and smooth coating. You hang the products on the production line before they are powder coated. After coating, you remove them from the line and check the quality.Your work is an important final step in the production process. You make sure the products are clean, complete and ready for the customer. You will receive clear instructions and support from experienced colleagues. This makes the job suitable for someone with production experience, but also for someone who wants to learn a new technical skill. What will you do?
- Hang metal products on the production line;
- Remove finished products after powder coating;
- Check products for damage and coating quality;
- Clean and lightly sand products;
- Carry out small finishing tasks;
- Report problems to your supervisor;
- Keep your workplace clean and safe.

You work in a two-shift schedule:
- Morning shift: 06:00 – 14:30;
- Evening shift: 14:30 – 23:00.

   Wat we je bieden - A gross hourly wage starting from €15,02;
- A job for 24 to 40 hours per week;
- 25 vacation days based on full-time employment;
- 8.33% holiday allowance;
- Travel expense reimbursement;
- The opportunity to learn powder coating and other production skills;
- A friendly team and a clear working schedule.

At Start People, we use equal pay. This means that your employment conditions match those of colleagues who work directly for the client. This can include vacation days, shift allowance, ADV compensation and other benefits.
   Functie-eisen You do not need years of experience. It is more important that you enjoy practical work and are willing to learn. You:
- Like working with your hands;
- Work carefully and check the quality of your work;
- Are comfortable with standing, walking and active work;
- Are available for the two-shift schedule;
- Can work independently and as part of a team;
- Speak Dutch, English or German well enough to understand safet
